# Intentionally empty.
#
# Grafana scans /etc/grafana/provisioning/{datasources,dashboards,plugins,
# alerting} at start-up and logs an ERROR for any that is missing. Because the
# whole provisioning tree is bind-mounted read-only from the host, a directory
# absent here is absent in the container -- which produced two error-level
# lines on every boot:
#
#   level=error msg="Failed to read plugin provisioning files from directory"
#
# Nothing is broken by those lines, but an error in the log of a monitoring
# stack is exactly the wrong thing to teach an operator to ignore. Keeping the
# directory present and empty silences them. Git does not track empty
# directories, hence this file; Grafana only reads *.yaml/*.yml, so it ignores
# a dotfile.
